@page "/legend"

<PageTitle>Legend</PageTitle>

<section class="legend-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Knowledge</p>
    <h1>How this RAG works</h1>
    <p>
        Retrieval-augmented generation: retrieve your own passages, put them in the prompt, then generate.
        The model answers from those slices, not from training memory. A C# Policy layer can still Deny after the last token.
    </p>

    <h2>Official flow</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><strong>Prepare (ingest)</strong> — chunk text, embed each chunk, store text + vector + source. <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/dotnet/ai/conceptual/rag">.NET RAG</a></li>
        <li><strong>Retrieve</strong> — embed the question; nearest vectors in the index are the candidate passages. <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry/concepts/retrieval-augmented-generation">Foundry RAG</a></li>
        <li><strong>Augment</strong> — those <em>texts</em> (not the vectors) go into the prompt as grounding data.</li>
        <li><strong>Generate</strong> — the chat model writes from that prompt; citations come from stored source metadata.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What this app actually stores</h2>
    <p>
        A row in <code>InMemoryDocumentIndex</code> is <code>PolicyChunkRecord</code>: id, source filename, chunk text, embedding.
        Collection <code>policy-chunks</code> is the vector store (cosine). List <code>_all</code> is a copy used as hybrid fallback.
        Seed files are short, so a 640-token window with overlap 96 usually keeps the whole file as one chunk.
    </p>

    <h2>Terms</h2>
    <dl>
        <dt>Chunk</dt>
        <dd>A slice of a document, sized for the embedder and the prompt. Here: max 640 tokens, overlap 96 if a split happens.</dd>
        <dt>Embedding</dt>
        <dd>A list of floats that represents meaning. Similar text sits close. This app: <code>nomic-embed-text</code>, 768 dimensions. Search uses cosine similarity. <a href="https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/embeddings">OpenAI embeddings</a></dd>
        <dt>Index</dt>
        <dd>The store of chunks + embeddings, optimized for retrieval. Prototype: in-process RAM, not Azure AI Search.</dd>
        <dt>Hybrid</dt>
        <dd>Vector neighbors, then a word-overlap filter so a high cosine with no shared terms is dropped.</dd>
        <dt>Citation</dt>
        <dd>Which source file a retrieved chunk came from — metadata stored next to the text.</dd>
        <dt>Stub</dt>
        <dd>A stand-in when Ollama is offline. Not an LLM — copied sentences so the app still runs.</dd>
        <dt>Allow</dt>
        <dd>Grounded answer with citations and no hard conflict.</dd>
        <dt>Deny</dt>
        <dd>Blocked by Policy (secrets, bypass, prohibited gifts, …).</dd>
        <dt>NeedsHuman</dt>
        <dd>Retrieved chunks disagree on a number (refund days, PTO, $ caps).</dd>
        <dt>Refuse</dt>
        <dd>Nothing relevant in the index — the model must not invent policy.</dd>
    </dl>

    <h2>Modules</h2>
    <dl>
        <dt>Ingestion</dt>
        <dd>Turns files into chunks + embeddings. Hosted inside Web.</dd>
        <dt>Assistant</dt>
        <dd>Ask + Policy inside Web. Streams tokens; evals still wait for the final Answer.</dd>
    </dl>
</section>
